  "Question": "After Sally takes \\(20\\) shots, she has made \\(55\\%\\) of her shots. After she takes \\(5\\) more shots, she raises her percentage to \\(56\\%.\\) How many of the last \\(5\\) shots did she make?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The percentages refer to different numbers of attempts, so first convert each percentage into a number of made shots. In her first \\(20\\) attempts, Sally made\n\\[\n0.55\\times20=11\n\\]\nshots. After the next \\(5\\) attempts, she had taken \\(25\\) shots altogether and made\n\\[\n0.56\\times25=14.\n\\]\nThe increase in her made-shot total is \\(14-11=3\\). Therefore she made \\(3\\) of the last five shots, choice C.",
